# Write paths: a deep nested copy

`[:Class | path = expr]` rebuilds only the objects on the path. This world is
six composition levels down to the fountain, with an ocean sitting beside the
continent so a deep write can prove siblings stay put.

Construction is still the full positional picture. Methods use write-paths.

## Schema

```
World = Continent Ocean
Continent = Country
Country = Capital
Capital = Plaza
Plaza = Fountain
Fountain = Int/jets String/name
Ocean = Int/depth
```

## Construction

```
[:World
  [:Continent
    [:Country
      [:Capital
        [:Plaza
          [:Fountain 7 "Triton"]]]]]
  [:Ocean 4000]
]
```

## Methods

```
Fountain::rename = { String/n | [:Fountain | name = n] }

World::moreJets = {
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets = (continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets + 1)]
}

World::renameFountain = { String/n |
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.name = n]
}

World::deeperOcean = {
  [:World | ocean.depth = (ocean.depth + 100)]
}

World::resize = {
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets = 12, ocean.depth = 5000]
}

World::boostFountain = { Fountain/f |
  [:Fountain f | jets = (f.jets + 1)]
}

World::label = {
  f = continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.
  jets = f.jets.
  depth = ocean.depth.
  "Fountain {name} has {jets} jets; ocean {depth} deep.".tpl({String:String "name": f.name, "jets": jets.str(), "depth": depth.str()})
}
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var world = WorldAssemblage.factory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(world.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("moreJets");
    trace(world.moreJets().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("renameFountain");
    trace(world.renameFountain("Arethusa").toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("deeperOcean");
    trace(world.deeperOcean().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("resize");
    trace(world.resize().toConstruction(0, helper));
}
```
